# Catalog query packages

Follow the project skill `.cursor/skills/add-catalog-query/SKILL.md`.

- One folder per domain: `core/database/<domain>/` (see `users/`). Functions take `*database.Catalog` and `DB()`.
- Do not add per-table files to `core/database/` or methods on `Catalog`. Domain errors stay in the table package.
- DDL still goes through catalog migrations, not query packages. The same PR registers the table and its FKs in `catalogmodel` — `.cursor/skills/add-catalog-model/SKILL.md`.
- Official resource / vocab `Delete` goes through `deleteimpact` — see `.cursor/skills/add-catalog-delete/SKILL.md` and `.cursor/rules/catalog-deletes.mdc`.
- Researcher callers obtain `*database.Catalog` from `catalogsession.Do` / FFI `withProjectCatalog`, not open-per-call. See `.cursor/skills/use-catalog-session/SKILL.md`.
- An open-catalog read of the canonical graph follows a `hops.Hop` with `graphcache.Graph.Follow`. Do not hand-write the association join in SQL; the bridge shape lives in the connectrules registry.
- `canonicalgraph.Walk` stays for dependent discovery and for any walk that must see rows the cache has not loaded, including inside a write. `WalkSource` stays for one Source.
